      "body": "## Why\nThe gate required an exact \"2.15.0\" match, so nightly/dev installs\n(2.15.0.devYYYYMMDD) silently skipped all pipelining backports\n(#199884, #200238, #200199): no error, no log line. Schedules then\nbehave differently between an RC and a dev build of the same release,\nwhich is costly to diagnose.\n## What changed\nRelax the gate to startswith(\"2.15.0\") so dev builds load the backports\ntoo. Safety is unchanged:\n- each function edit is anchored by before/after sha256 of the target\n  source, so a dev build whose source drifted fails explicitly with the\n  \"revalidate compatibility backport\" error instead of being patched\n  blindly;\n- TORCHTITAN_DISABLE_TORCH_COMPAT=1 still opts out process-wide.\n## Testing\nOn torch 2.15.0.dev20261005: the startup warning confirms the\ncompatibility backports now apply, and fsdp2_pp2_deferred (4 GPUs),\nlooped_bfs and interleaved_1f1b (2 GPUs) pass 10 training steps with\nexpected loss and grad_norm.",
      "changedFiles": 1,
